WEBVTT

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.209
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:03.169
You gotta let that guy know, back off.

00:00:03.377 --> 00:00:06.045
That is Marissa's letter.
That you stole from her locker?

00:00:06.254 --> 00:00:07.463
If she finds out, you guys are done.

00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:10.006
- The interior design job, I want it.
- We've found our girl.

00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:12.299
Am I dating the female me?
Like me, but as a girl?

00:00:12.508 --> 00:00:14.592
People can be really unpredictable.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.093
I can't believe you stole it.

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.053
How can you say
he's not in love with you?

00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:19.512
I can't do this anymore.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:21.930
You and Marissa aren't supposed
to be together.

00:00:22.139 --> 00:00:25.016
- I am not gonna let this happen.
- Who's gonna believe you?

00:00:26.475 --> 00:00:28.601
Stay away from her!

00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:41.359
You're not having breakfast?

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.527
Not really hungry.

00:00:44.486 --> 00:00:49.031
Dr. Kim just called to let us know
that you've been suspended, indefinitely.

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:50.823
Until the disciplinary committee...

00:00:51.032 --> 00:00:53.200
...can figure out whether or not
they want to expel you.

00:00:53.408 --> 00:00:56.369
I know you want me to say I'm sorry,
but I'm not.

00:00:56.577 --> 00:00:58.286
Oliver admitted it. Right to my face.

00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:01.038
He told me he wanted me gone
so he could get to Marissa.

00:01:01.622 --> 00:01:04.290
Then why would he drop
the assault charges against you?

00:01:06.458 --> 00:01:08.001
- He did that?
- Yeah.

00:01:08.209 --> 00:01:10.878
I mean, it seems to me
that if he had it in for you...

00:01:11.086 --> 00:01:13.754
...if he wanted you gone,
you'd be back in juvie already.

00:01:13.921 --> 00:01:15.839
I mean, you know that, right?

00:01:17.757 --> 00:01:19.758
Come on, help me out here, would you?

00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:22.093
Tell me what's going on.

00:01:23.552 --> 00:01:24.845
Oliver's dangerous.

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:27.805
This is what I know:

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.974
You attacked him. Period.
You're on probation.

00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:35.101
You knew the slightest infraction would
result in you being taken from us.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.061
And you did it anyway.

00:01:37.269 --> 00:01:39.937
For the life of me,
I can't understand why.

00:01:40.146 --> 00:01:41.689
Talk to me.

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:44.357
Come on, Ryan, talk to me.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.525
What's the point?
You won't believe me.

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:48.985
It's not about what I believe.
I wish it was.

00:01:49.193 --> 00:01:51.153
It's about what you did.

00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:54.822
The next time you feel
like raising your fist...

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.282
...you had better open your mouth
and talk.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.742
I'm here for that.

00:02:08.497 --> 00:02:10.290
What am I supposed to do?

00:02:10.498 --> 00:02:13.750
I can't ground you.
I'm not gonna chain you to the wall.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.794
You want to go after that Oliver kid?

00:02:17.628 --> 00:02:21.005
Go ahead. The door's open.

00:02:22.422 --> 00:02:26.550
But if you want to stay,
if you want to be part of this family...

00:02:26.758 --> 00:02:29.010
...you're not gonna go anywhere
or do anything...

00:02:29.218 --> 00:02:32.304
...you're not gonna see anyone,
unless Kirsten and I say it's okay.

00:02:32.512 --> 00:02:34.180
That's the deal.
Take it or leave it.

00:03:41.513 --> 00:03:43.640
So Ryan just, like,
punched him for no reason?

00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:45.683
That's what Ryan does.
He punches people.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:48.726
He doesn't talk to them,
and he doesn't listen.

00:03:48.935 --> 00:03:50.394
He had to have a reason, though.

00:03:50.602 --> 00:03:53.938
I mean, yeah, Ryan's violent,
but he's not stupid.

00:03:54.688 --> 00:03:56.064
He just...

00:03:56.231 --> 00:04:00.275
I don't know. He thinks Oliver's
in love with me or something.

00:04:00.442 --> 00:04:01.901
Well, isn't he?

00:04:02.068 --> 00:04:03.444
- A little?
- We're just friends.

00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:05.070
Okay!

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:08.364
I mean, Oliver's, like, the only guy
in my life who isn't jealous...

00:04:08.572 --> 00:04:11.240
...and scary and breathing
down my neck all the time.

00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:13.367
And he actually tells me
what he's thinking.

00:04:13.575 --> 00:04:14.951
Unlike some people.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:17.911
So are you and Ryan...?

00:04:18.703 --> 00:04:20.163
We broke up.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:21.789
Whoa, Coop.

00:04:24.082 --> 00:04:26.833
So that means that
we're both single now.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.209
Which...

00:04:28.418 --> 00:04:30.336
...rocks! Right?

00:04:30.544 --> 00:04:31.711
No more Ryan.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.964
No more Seth Cohen.
We're totally free. Liberated.

00:04:35.172 --> 00:04:39.216
In fact, how about I treat us both to
a little Burke Williams today after school?

00:04:39.425 --> 00:04:41.551
A little facial, a little massage...

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:44.553
I can't. I promised Oliver
I'd help him study after school.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.429
Oh. Well, how about this weekend?

00:04:46.637 --> 00:04:48.389
My dad's taking Kaitlin to my grandma's...

00:04:48.597 --> 00:04:50.682
...and I have to spend the weekend
at my mom's.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.642
Apparently, she's got this
mother-daughter marathon planned.

00:04:54.392 --> 00:04:58.103
- Well, then when are we gonna hang out?
- Soon.

00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:04.399
Hey, you coming?

00:05:07.025 --> 00:05:10.861
Well, even if Ryan gets expelled,
he's still gonna live with you guys, right?

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:13.738
- Your parents aren't gonna kick him out.
- No.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.489
I don't think so.

00:05:15.697 --> 00:05:17.073
Well, is he okay?

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.325
He's not the one
who got punched in the face.

00:05:19.533 --> 00:05:21.451
I'm talking about
in the larger sense, Seth.

00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:23.911
I guess. I don't really know.

00:05:25.704 --> 00:05:28.831
- Haven't you talked to him?
- No. What am I supposed to say?

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:32.083
I don't know. "Are you okay?"
"Is there anything I can do?"

00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:34.042
That's the thing.
There's nothing I can do.

00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:37.378
I begged him to stay away from Oliver,
and he didn't listen to me.

00:05:37.586 --> 00:05:40.588
Look, you don't know Ryan that well,
okay? You don't understand.

00:05:40.796 --> 00:05:42.464
I'm trying.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.051
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:50.386
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:05:53.179 --> 00:05:54.888
- How is everybody?
- Good.

00:05:55.097 --> 00:05:56.181
- Good.
- Good.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.015
Good.

00:06:01.643 --> 00:06:03.102
Okay, this is really...

00:06:03.269 --> 00:06:04.394
- Weird?
- Yeah.

00:06:04.603 --> 00:06:07.396
- Just because you and Ryan aren't...
- Doesn't mean we can't...

00:06:07.563 --> 00:06:08.856
- Exactly.
- Right.

00:06:10.898 --> 00:06:14.109
- So is he okay?
- What up? What up?

00:06:14.526 --> 00:06:16.235
So, what are we doing this weekend?

00:06:16.444 --> 00:06:17.736
Ski trip? Mammoth?

00:06:17.945 --> 00:06:20.529
Six to 8 inches
of fresh powder tomorrow.

00:06:20.738 --> 00:06:21.822
Oliver, your lip.

00:06:22.989 --> 00:06:26.158
I was hoping it had already made
the transition from scary to sexy.

00:06:27.576 --> 00:06:28.868
Not yet, huh?

00:06:29.077 --> 00:06:31.953
- Walk you to Western civ?
- Sure.

00:06:32.162 --> 00:06:34.622
- Bye, you guys.
- Bye.

00:06:37.415 --> 00:06:40.000
- Wow. Oliver seems almost...
- Happy?

00:06:40.208 --> 00:06:44.336
Yeah, well, why shouldn't he?
He has Marissa all to himself now.

00:06:47.963 --> 00:06:49.423
What?

00:06:51.674 --> 00:06:53.717
I think I made a mistake.

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:58.011
- By leaving Ryan home alone?
- By bringing him home in the first place.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.555
Sandy, he's a good kid.
He's not perfect.

00:07:00.763 --> 00:07:03.807
But we'll work it out. We always do.
Everything's gonna be okay.

00:07:04.015 --> 00:07:06.308
Who'd have ever thought
you'd be telling me that?

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:09.435
- Kirsten Cohen?
- Yes.

00:07:09.644 --> 00:07:11.186
- You shouldn't be here.
- I'm sorry?

00:07:11.395 --> 00:07:13.938
We have a work order from Julie Cooper.
Excuse me, sir.

00:07:14.855 --> 00:07:16.898
There must be a mistake.

00:07:17.523 --> 00:07:19.858
What are you doing here?
You were going to lunch.

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.735
- We ordered in. Deli?
- Oh, hi, Sandy. No, thank you.

00:07:22.902 --> 00:07:24.611
Julie, what is going on?

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.113
Well, as the Newport Group's
new design director...

00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.948
...I've decided to give the office
a much-needed facelift.

00:07:30.115 --> 00:07:33.283
Wait till you see your furniture, Kiki.
It's very fresh. Very Danish.

00:07:33.492 --> 00:07:35.034
- Very "hello."
- I'm sure it is...

00:07:35.201 --> 00:07:37.369
...but you can't just initiate a redesign.

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:39.912
- You need approvals.
- Caleb said it was okay.

00:07:40.121 --> 00:07:41.997
Oh, if Caleb said it was okay...

00:07:44.332 --> 00:07:45.499
My coffee table!

00:07:45.708 --> 00:07:48.043
Kiki, what's going on?
Some man in a jumpsuit...

00:07:48.251 --> 00:07:50.085
...just made off with my massage chair.

00:07:50.294 --> 00:07:53.129
I want my chair. I want my desk.
I want my office back.

00:07:53.296 --> 00:07:56.214
By the time we get back from lunch,
you'll have it and love it.

00:07:56.673 --> 00:07:58.883
You want to join us to celebrate
my new position?

00:07:59.216 --> 00:08:00.759
Oh, I'm not gonna touch that one.

00:08:01.343 --> 00:08:04.094
- No, we're okay.
- Okay.

00:08:07.179 --> 00:08:09.181
I have work to do.

00:08:09.389 --> 00:08:13.934
Don't worry, honey. You said it yourself.
Everything's gonna be fine.

00:08:41.368 --> 00:08:43.410
Come on. You have to go.

00:08:43.619 --> 00:08:46.079
We both could use the weekend away.
It'll be my treat.

00:08:46.287 --> 00:08:48.956
I can't. Besides, I'm the one
who should be treating you.

00:08:49.164 --> 00:08:51.457
You wouldn't have gotten hurt
if it weren't for me.

00:08:51.666 --> 00:08:53.041
Hey, that was Ryan, not you.

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:55.168
What did we learn in therapy?

00:08:55.543 --> 00:08:58.628
Say it with me now.
"We are responsible for our own actions."

00:08:59.546 --> 00:09:01.005
Hey, what's up?

00:09:01.172 --> 00:09:03.840
Luke, help me convince Marissa
to come to Mammoth with us.

00:09:04.007 --> 00:09:05.549
- Who's going to Mammoth?
- Not me.

00:09:05.716 --> 00:09:08.176
My dad's out of town,
so I'm gonna be at my mom's.

00:09:08.384 --> 00:09:11.845
Which means she'll be next to Ryan,
which is not good for her right now.

00:09:12.053 --> 00:09:16.306
- Well, isn't that kind of up to Marissa?
- Look, it's not a big deal. It's fine.

00:09:16.514 --> 00:09:19.975
Okay, so let me at least get you
and your mom a suite at the hotel.

00:09:20.392 --> 00:09:23.811
That way I'll be there, and you won't
even have to think about Ryan.

00:09:25.061 --> 00:09:28.647
Look, this is probably her now,
already checking up on me.

00:09:32.691 --> 00:09:35.943
- It's Ryan, isn't it?
- You're not gonna get it?

00:09:36.152 --> 00:09:38.695
- She's not talking to Ryan.
- Is she talking to me?

00:09:38.903 --> 00:09:41.030
- Or are you doing her talking now?
- Luke, don't.

00:09:41.238 --> 00:09:43.073
- Marissa...
- I should probably just go.

00:09:43.281 --> 00:09:44.740
Stay.

00:09:45.241 --> 00:09:47.242
You two enjoy your lunch.

00:09:50.244 --> 00:09:51.953
I am so sorry.

00:09:53.704 --> 00:09:56.748
I guess I can just get a little
overprotective sometimes.

00:09:56.956 --> 00:10:00.834
- But I would never presume to...
- I know. It's okay. Really.

00:10:02.543 --> 00:10:05.003
Why don't I just go get us some dessert.

00:10:19.679 --> 00:10:21.222
You have one new message.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.391
Hey, I was hoping maybe we could talk,
face to face, if you want.

00:10:25.599 --> 00:10:28.726
So I'll meet you in the library
after school, and I hope...

00:10:28.935 --> 00:10:31.061
I'll see you there.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.773
To save the message, press two.
To erase the message, press three.

00:10:37.774 --> 00:10:39.775
Message deleted.

00:10:44.903 --> 00:10:48.238
So, what's the plan? Comic books first?
Or frozen yogurt?

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:50.865
You think it's cool
if we do the comics run tomorrow?

00:10:51.074 --> 00:10:53.825
I thought it'd be better
if I went home to check on Ryan.

00:10:53.992 --> 00:10:57.578
Yeah, that's a good idea.
Do you want some company?

00:10:57.744 --> 00:11:00.788
- Hey. Where are you guys going?
- Well, we were talking about...

00:11:00.996 --> 00:11:03.957
...maybe going to the comic-book store...
- Really?

00:11:04.916 --> 00:11:06.500
Can I come?

00:11:06.792 --> 00:11:08.334
To the comic-book store?

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.753
Yeah. I like comics. Sort of.

00:11:10.961 --> 00:11:12.587
You do?

00:11:12.795 --> 00:11:15.756
Believe it or not, Betty and Veronica
had a huge influence on me.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.591
You know what, I do believe that.

00:11:19.258 --> 00:11:20.550
I believe it too.

00:11:20.759 --> 00:11:23.594
Besides, Marissa has Oliver now...

00:11:23.802 --> 00:11:27.388
...and I have a whole afternoon to kill.

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:31.557
So, great.

00:11:31.766 --> 00:11:33.308
- You'll spend it with us.
- Yeah.

00:11:34.309 --> 00:11:36.560
Except, don't you have to go
check on Ryan?

00:11:36.894 --> 00:11:38.061
Well, I...

00:11:41.313 --> 00:11:42.856
Excuse me.

00:11:43.273 --> 00:11:44.732
Hey. What are you doing here?

00:11:44.899 --> 00:11:47.901
- I'm supposed to meet Marissa.
- Okay, but here? In broad daylight?

00:11:48.109 --> 00:11:51.153
- In front of God, Dr. Kim and everyone?
- She's not taking my calls.

00:11:51.361 --> 00:11:53.279
This is the only place
I knew I could see her.

00:11:53.488 --> 00:11:54.822
Does Marissa know about this?

00:11:55.364 --> 00:11:57.532
You'd think you, of all people,
would believe me.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.283
Ryan, Marissa's a big girl.

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:01.951
You can't tell her who
she can and can't hang out with.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:05.954
Oliver's not stable. He's dangerous. One
girl got a restraining order against him.

00:12:06.162 --> 00:12:08.705
Natalie? Either she lives
in Niagara Falls or doesn't exist.

00:12:08.914 --> 00:12:12.166
- I'm sure he's not making up girlfriends.
- Seth, he's crazy.

00:12:12.374 --> 00:12:14.834
Okay. Okay. Fine. He's crazy.

00:12:15.043 --> 00:12:17.044
But this Mission: Impossible
act you're pulling...

00:12:17.252 --> 00:12:20.880
...it's not the way to make your case.
- I have to go.

00:12:34.013 --> 00:12:35.681
She's not coming.

00:12:37.056 --> 00:12:40.725
She asked me to tell you not to call her
anymore and not to try and see her.

00:12:40.934 --> 00:12:43.477
If you do, she'll get a restraining order
against you.

00:12:43.686 --> 00:12:46.604
- Really? What's that like?
- It's not my fault she won't see you.

00:12:46.813 --> 00:12:49.398
I mean, you spied on her.
You stole from her.

00:12:49.606 --> 00:12:52.775
- You beat up one of her best friends.
- I'd do it again too. Right now.

00:12:52.983 --> 00:12:56.610
I could've pressed charges, but I didn't.
I'm trying to help you.

00:12:56.819 --> 00:13:00.113
But if you keep this up,
no one's gonna be able to save you.

00:13:00.321 --> 00:13:03.198
Give it up, buddy. It's over.

00:13:07.367 --> 00:13:09.160
Hey, Oliver.

00:13:10.327 --> 00:13:11.578
It hasn't even begun.

00:13:22.251 --> 00:13:24.920
I need my office back
by the end of the day, Brian.

00:13:25.128 --> 00:13:28.755
If Julie Cooper asks you to do anything
else, you nod your head and do nothing.

00:13:28.964 --> 00:13:30.173
Thanks.

00:13:30.381 --> 00:13:32.174
- Have you seen the coffee?
- Very funny.

00:13:32.383 --> 00:13:35.676
- In the meantime, I have no place to work.
- Yeah, I have no place to eat.

00:13:35.885 --> 00:13:39.429
Her first day, and Julie has displaced
half the staff from their offices...

00:13:39.637 --> 00:13:43.515
...and personally alienated the other half.
She's driving everyone crazy.

00:13:43.723 --> 00:13:46.433
Including me. Please talk to her,
before I starve to death.

00:13:46.642 --> 00:13:49.769
You can't talk to Julie Cooper.
She's Julie Cooper.

00:13:49.977 --> 00:13:52.145
Talk to your dad.
He's the reason she's there.

00:13:52.354 --> 00:13:55.189
I know, but then he'll think
it's personal or that I'm jealous.

00:13:55.397 --> 00:13:57.107
I can't talk to my father.

00:13:57.315 --> 00:13:59.900
You don't mind if I work
out of the house, do you?

00:14:00.984 --> 00:14:03.944
- Sorry, I thought if there was coffee...
- Oh, Ryan, come on in.

00:14:04.153 --> 00:14:06.738
There's coffee and cereal and...

00:14:07.905 --> 00:14:09.698
...a model home.

00:14:09.906 --> 00:14:12.199
Yeah. Okay. Thanks.

00:14:19.412 --> 00:14:21.622
He didn't leave the pool house
all day yesterday.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:24.374
- Maybe we're being too hard on him.
- We gotta hang tough.

00:14:24.582 --> 00:14:28.126
- It's for his own good.
- Then why do I feel so bad?

00:14:29.669 --> 00:14:31.837
Kirsten. You're not dressed.

00:14:32.045 --> 00:14:33.796
- Julie.
- We could carpool from now on.

00:14:34.005 --> 00:14:36.464
We're next door.
Have you read the latest EPA figures?

00:14:36.673 --> 00:14:40.133
What we're doing to the environment?
Sandy, I can see you hiding.

00:14:40.342 --> 00:14:42.552
Not hiding, Julie.
Just making myself presentable.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:45.095
- Don't go to any trouble for me.
- Don't worry.

00:14:45.303 --> 00:14:46.971
Kirsten, you're still not dressed.

00:14:47.179 --> 00:14:52.183
Yes, well, I was planning on working from
the house today, since my office is still...

00:14:52.391 --> 00:14:54.809
Honey, weren't you supposed
to meet with Caleb...

00:14:55.018 --> 00:14:57.561
...to talk about the thing?

00:14:58.562 --> 00:15:00.771
- It can wait.
- So can Julie. Grab a shower.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.106
- I can get Julie some coffee.
- I'll help myself.

00:15:03.315 --> 00:15:05.149
- Is it flavored?
- No.

00:15:05.358 --> 00:15:07.192
Go ahead. Go.

00:15:16.573 --> 00:15:18.032
Aren't you late for school?

00:15:18.991 --> 00:15:22.285
- I got suspended.
- Oh, what a surprise.

00:15:22.493 --> 00:15:24.911
Who'd you beat up this time? Dr. Kim?

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.496
I guess you and Marissa
haven't talked in a while.

00:15:28.497 --> 00:15:31.832
Well, as a matter of fact,
she'll be spending the weekend with me.

00:15:32.041 --> 00:15:33.125
She will?

00:15:33.667 --> 00:15:35.918
I guess you and Marissa
haven't talked in a while.

00:15:39.754 --> 00:15:43.882
Look, I know you and I haven't always
agreed when it comes to Marissa...

00:15:44.048 --> 00:15:47.050
...but I'm asking you, please,
keep her away from this kid Oliver.

00:15:47.842 --> 00:15:49.969
He's not well.

00:15:50.219 --> 00:15:51.762
Really?

00:15:53.471 --> 00:15:55.806
The boy who lives in the pool house
is warning me...

00:15:56.014 --> 00:15:58.766
...about the boy
who lives in the penthouse?

00:15:59.641 --> 00:16:01.184
He's got this thing that he does.

00:16:01.351 --> 00:16:03.936
He locks into a girl,
thinks she'll make everything okay.

00:16:04.144 --> 00:16:05.937
And when she can't, he loses it.

00:16:06.146 --> 00:16:08.981
I am not getting involved
in the throes of teenage romance.

00:16:09.147 --> 00:16:11.399
He cut his wrists last year
because of a girl.

00:16:11.607 --> 00:16:13.734
When his girlfriend Natalie
broke up with him...

00:16:13.942 --> 00:16:16.360
...he got busted for trying to buy cocaine.

00:16:16.569 --> 00:16:17.945
It's true. You can ask Marissa.

00:16:20.238 --> 00:16:23.406
- Julie, you ready?
- Yeah.

00:16:25.741 --> 00:16:27.450
Stay out of trouble, Ryan.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.749
- What did your mom say about Mammoth?
- I didn't ask her yet.

00:16:40.292 --> 00:16:41.834
I'm sorry. I just...

00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:45.087
I try not to talk to my mom
as much as possible.

00:16:45.295 --> 00:16:48.672
Look, if you don't want to hang out
with me this weekend, that's fine.

00:16:48.881 --> 00:16:50.840
- What?
- It's okay if you don't.

00:16:51.049 --> 00:16:54.592
Just tell me. Because after
what happened with me and Natalie...

00:16:54.801 --> 00:16:57.219
I do want to hang out with you.

00:16:57.428 --> 00:17:01.097
Believe me, there's nothing I'd rather do
than just blow everything off...

00:17:01.305 --> 00:17:04.140
...school, therapy, my mom,
and hang out with you.

00:17:04.932 --> 00:17:06.517
- But I've got so...
- You mean it?

00:17:06.934 --> 00:17:08.476
Seriously?

00:17:09.644 --> 00:17:11.603
Then let's do it.
Let's blow it off.

00:17:11.812 --> 00:17:13.229
All right. We can drive to L.A.

00:17:13.396 --> 00:17:17.357
We can have lunch at the Ivy,
do the Getty, swing by the Troubadour.

00:17:18.149 --> 00:17:21.401
It sounds perfect,
except my mom would kill me.

00:17:21.609 --> 00:17:23.819
I'm supposed to have dinner
with her tonight.

00:17:24.028 --> 00:17:26.070
What if I get you back by dinner?

00:17:26.279 --> 00:17:29.531
- Come on. You know you want to.
- Stop it.

00:17:29.739 --> 00:17:32.199
- What about therapy?
- Oh, you don't need therapy.

00:17:32.408 --> 00:17:35.827
From what you told me, your mom's
the one who needs therapy, right?

00:17:37.161 --> 00:17:39.329
Promise I'll be back before dinner?

00:17:48.376 --> 00:17:50.294
- Where are they going?
- I don't know.

00:17:50.502 --> 00:17:53.254
- But I don't trust that dude.
- Stop it. You sound like Ryan.

00:17:55.005 --> 00:17:57.882
- You've met Natalie, right?
- Oliver's ex, Natalie?

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.466
No. You?

00:18:00.592 --> 00:18:02.802
No. Ryan thinks he made her up.

00:18:07.471 --> 00:18:11.224
Oliver said she went to Pacific, right?
I've got friends there. I can just ask.

00:18:11.432 --> 00:18:14.726
- You don't think that's a little crazy?
- Dude, have you met Oliver?

00:18:17.769 --> 00:18:21.689
- Dad, do you have a minute?
- Exactly one.

00:18:23.231 --> 00:18:24.690
It's about Julie.

00:18:27.651 --> 00:18:29.277
Close the door.

00:18:34.613 --> 00:18:36.615
She's driving me crazy.

00:18:36.823 --> 00:18:39.700
- Excuse me?
- Don't get me wrong, I enjoy the woman.

00:18:39.908 --> 00:18:43.702
But not every living minute of the day.
She's there every time I turn around.

00:18:43.911 --> 00:18:47.580
At home, in the office. I wouldn't
be surprised if she wasn't in here now.

00:18:47.788 --> 00:18:49.373
Dad, you're the one who hired her.

00:18:49.748 --> 00:18:52.333
I gave her something to do,
so she'd stop calling me.

00:18:52.541 --> 00:18:55.710
Well, it worked. Now she doesn't
have to call you. She's always here.

00:18:55.918 --> 00:18:58.920
Which is why I want you to talk to her.
I know she's your friend...

00:18:59.129 --> 00:19:02.964
...but in the interest of the business,
not to mention your father's sanity...

00:19:03.173 --> 00:19:04.882
...this has to end.

00:19:05.091 --> 00:19:06.800
What are you talking about?
The job?

00:19:09.218 --> 00:19:12.262
- You want me to break up with her?
- I knew you'd understand.

00:19:21.434 --> 00:19:22.643
Hey.

00:19:23.477 --> 00:19:25.770
So Summer and Anna are both here.

00:19:25.979 --> 00:19:29.606
Summer is about to read her first comic.
I knew you wouldn't want to miss that.

00:19:29.814 --> 00:19:31.482
Let me know how it goes.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.193
Okay. Well, I can see you're busy.

00:19:35.401 --> 00:19:37.236
Why don't you invite over Oliver?

00:19:37.861 --> 00:19:41.363
- Natalie, if you can find her.
- Yeah. Maybe I'll do that.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.201
- Hey, guys. What are you doing?
- Hey.

00:19:48.409 --> 00:19:51.661
Believe it or not, Summer has shown
a latent interest in comic bookery.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.871
- I don't believe it.
- Believe it.

00:19:56.331 --> 00:19:58.374
- Where's Ryan?
- I invited him to join us...

00:19:58.582 --> 00:20:00.667
...but he's staying
in the Fortress of Solitude.

00:20:00.876 --> 00:20:03.127
- Superman reference.
- I knew that.

00:20:04.128 --> 00:20:06.337
So I'm gonna start you off
with some basics:

00:20:06.546 --> 00:20:08.672
Batman: The Dark Knight Returns.
Very important.

00:20:08.881 --> 00:20:10.882
Watchman and The Sandman.

00:20:11.257 --> 00:20:12.633
Enjoy.

00:20:12.883 --> 00:20:14.050
- Seth?
- Yeah.

00:20:14.259 --> 00:20:17.219
Don't you want to start
on something less grim and gritty?

00:20:17.428 --> 00:20:19.887
- Like what?
- Like the Archies?

00:20:20.638 --> 00:20:21.847
Anna. The Archies?

00:20:22.055 --> 00:20:26.016
Hey, I'm with Anna. Life's gritty enough.
Comic books are for fun.

00:20:26.433 --> 00:20:28.560
Life's gritty enough?
We live in Newport Beach.

00:20:30.519 --> 00:20:32.812
- Hey, Mr. Cohen?
- Yes?

00:20:33.021 --> 00:20:35.022
Did you read comic books
when you were a kid?

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:38.774
- Oh, yeah. Sure. I mean, not like Seth.
- I know.

00:20:38.983 --> 00:20:42.026
You have no idea how rare it is
to find another comic-book person.

00:20:42.235 --> 00:20:44.986
Especially one who loves Death Cab
and sailing.

00:20:45.153 --> 00:20:48.614
- I thought I was the only one.
- I thought Seth was the only one.

00:20:48.989 --> 00:20:50.823
Death Cab is a band, yes?

00:20:51.282 --> 00:20:53.325
Guys? Seth!

00:20:53.617 --> 00:20:56.994
- Can you help me with the groceries?
- Yeah, yeah. In a minute.

00:20:57.369 --> 00:21:00.246
So I guess you and Mrs. Cohen
have a lot in common, huh?

00:21:00.454 --> 00:21:04.332
Oh, yeah, sure. We both love...

00:21:06.542 --> 00:21:09.919
...Seth. So I guess we don't
have a lot in common.

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:17.048
Well, then what do you think is the key
to a successful relationship?

00:21:17.257 --> 00:21:19.466
The sooner we get the bags,
the sooner we eat.

00:21:19.675 --> 00:21:21.051
Coming.

00:21:21.217 --> 00:21:24.428
Well, I think as far as Cohen men
are concerned, the key...

00:21:24.636 --> 00:21:27.471
...is patience.
- Patience?

00:21:28.263 --> 00:21:30.640
Hey, Dad. Is it cool if Summer
stays for dinner?

00:21:33.684 --> 00:21:36.143
- I'm gonna get the groceries.
- All right. Thanks.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.897
- Come on, man. What are you doing?
- What are you doing?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.858
These are crazy people.

00:21:46.525 --> 00:21:49.610
Luke! What are you doing here?
Besides relieving me of grocery duty.

00:21:49.819 --> 00:21:52.987
I hadn't seen Ryan in a while,
so I thought I'd stop by and say hey.

00:21:53.196 --> 00:21:54.280
Is that okay?

00:21:54.572 --> 00:21:56.823
I can't stay.
I have to go have dinner with my dad.

00:21:57.031 --> 00:21:59.950
- But there's something you should know.
- What?

00:22:00.158 --> 00:22:02.660
I saw Marissa leave school today
with Oliver.

00:22:02.868 --> 00:22:05.829
They skipped the whole day.
And I tried her on her cell, but...

00:22:06.037 --> 00:22:07.913
- You don't know where they went?
- No.

00:22:08.455 --> 00:22:13.125
And I'm sure she's probably fine, right?
But there's something about that kid.

00:22:14.251 --> 00:22:16.002
So I went over to Pacific after school.

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:17.920
I know guys
on the water-polo team there.

00:22:18.128 --> 00:22:19.671
I figured I'd ask what they knew.

00:22:19.837 --> 00:22:21.880
What was he like
when he went to Pacific?

00:22:22.089 --> 00:22:24.173
Did they even know him?
Did they know Natalie?

00:22:24.715 --> 00:22:26.091
Well, it turns out...

00:22:26.842 --> 00:22:28.718
...there is no Natalie.

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:32.262
At least not at Pacific High.

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:42.852
- Are you sure it's okay that I'm staying?
- Oh, absolutely.

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:44.978
We have more than enough
for everybody.

00:22:45.187 --> 00:22:47.396
I don't know where
we're gonna put it all.

00:22:47.605 --> 00:22:49.856
Eventually, in my belly.

00:23:11.578 --> 00:23:13.996
- You go ahead and start without me.
- Okay.

00:23:14.997 --> 00:23:16.206
I'll go get Ryan.

00:23:21.001 --> 00:23:23.919
What are you doing at my house?
You have to leave. I mean it.

00:23:24.128 --> 00:23:26.421
- I have to tell you something.
- You went to my mom.

00:23:26.629 --> 00:23:29.839
She called the school. She called
the hotel looking for Oliver's parents.

00:23:30.048 --> 00:23:32.049
- Let me talk to you.
- Why do you hate him?

00:23:32.258 --> 00:23:33.508
What did he ever do to you?

00:23:34.259 --> 00:23:35.802
There is no Natalie.

00:23:36.344 --> 00:23:37.553
You're becoming pathetic.

00:23:37.761 --> 00:23:39.220
Ask him.

00:23:39.637 --> 00:23:42.681
Ask him to show you his yearbook.
She's not there. She's not real.

00:23:42.889 --> 00:23:44.098
He made her up.

00:23:44.307 --> 00:23:46.183
Marissa, inside.
You're in big trouble.

00:23:46.391 --> 00:23:49.060
- Ryan, go home.
- No. You know what, Ryan? You stay.

00:23:49.268 --> 00:23:50.436
I'm going.

00:23:50.644 --> 00:23:53.938
Marissa. Marissa, get back here!

00:23:54.813 --> 00:23:56.565
Get back here!

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:23.164
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:24:25.291 --> 00:24:27.876
Do you mind if I stay here tonight?

00:24:51.182 --> 00:24:52.975
I thought you might
want some breakfast.

00:24:53.183 --> 00:24:54.809
Thanks.

00:25:11.903 --> 00:25:14.113
I shouldn't have gone over
there last night.

00:25:15.781 --> 00:25:18.741
- Do you want to talk about it?
- Not really.

00:25:21.451 --> 00:25:22.827
Ryan...

00:25:24.328 --> 00:25:27.371
...I promise I will do everything
I can to help you.

00:25:27.580 --> 00:25:29.623
But I can't help you
if you don't talk to me.

00:25:30.123 --> 00:25:32.083
You don't tell me what's going on.

00:25:33.917 --> 00:25:36.335
Ryan, I thought you might like some...

00:25:37.169 --> 00:25:38.628
Coffee.

00:25:38.837 --> 00:25:41.505
- Great minds.
- Luke's here to see you.

00:25:48.176 --> 00:25:49.885
Thanks, you guys.

00:25:53.930 --> 00:25:55.222
Hey, man.

00:25:55.847 --> 00:25:58.307
So how did it go last night?
What'd she say?

00:25:58.516 --> 00:25:59.975
She didn't believe me.

00:26:00.183 --> 00:26:02.727
- Then her mom started in, and she ran.
- To Oliver's?

00:26:02.935 --> 00:26:04.478
I don't know.

00:26:04.978 --> 00:26:07.230
- So let's go find out.
- And then what?

00:26:07.438 --> 00:26:09.981
- She wants to be with him.
- You're just gonna give up?

00:26:10.190 --> 00:26:13.025
What else can I do?
She won't listen to a word I have to say.

00:26:13.233 --> 00:26:15.651
Well, she's gonna listen to me.

00:26:16.610 --> 00:26:18.320
See you.

00:26:27.284 --> 00:26:29.327
So if we leave for L.A.
After our massages...

00:26:29.535 --> 00:26:31.828
...we can check into my parents' suite
around 2.

00:26:32.787 --> 00:26:35.164
Wait. Your parents have
their own suite in L.A. Too?

00:26:35.372 --> 00:26:37.624
They have private suites
in all their hotels.

00:26:37.832 --> 00:26:40.750
- London, Paris...
- Oh, I wish we could go to Paris.

00:26:42.001 --> 00:26:44.419
We can. It's only 15 hours away.

00:26:45.128 --> 00:26:47.421
Yeah. As long as we're back
by Monday, right?

00:26:47.630 --> 00:26:51.090
Look, if you don't want to go,
just say so.

00:26:51.299 --> 00:26:53.884
- We don't have to.
- No, I do. I just can't.

00:26:54.092 --> 00:26:56.886
Why not? You've been saying you wanted
to get away from your mom...

00:26:57.052 --> 00:26:58.178
...and from Ryan.

00:26:58.595 --> 00:27:00.221
This way it'll just be you and me.

00:27:00.429 --> 00:27:01.722
In Paris.

00:27:02.973 --> 00:27:05.433
Hey, don't answer that.
It's probably your mom.

00:27:06.934 --> 00:27:08.393
It's Luke.

00:27:08.560 --> 00:27:10.311
- Hey.
- Marissa...

00:27:10.561 --> 00:27:12.562
- Where are you?
- I'm at the hotel.

00:27:12.770 --> 00:27:14.605
- Why is he calling?
- You gotta listen to me.

00:27:14.813 --> 00:27:16.690
There is no Natalie Bishop.

00:27:16.898 --> 00:27:18.733
- Ryan was right.
- Luke, don't you start.

00:27:18.983 --> 00:27:20.609
I'm trying to help you, Marissa.

00:27:20.817 --> 00:27:23.569
You want to help? Go to my mom's
and tell her I'm fine.

00:27:23.944 --> 00:27:26.029
- Marissa...
- Luke, please.

00:27:27.446 --> 00:27:29.364
I'll be there soon.

00:27:33.075 --> 00:27:34.743
He's just dropping off some clothes.

00:27:37.077 --> 00:27:38.495
If you don't want to stay...

00:27:38.703 --> 00:27:39.912
No, I do.

00:27:40.121 --> 00:27:42.873
I do. I just can't fly to Paris right now.

00:27:43.081 --> 00:27:44.665
I'm sorry.

00:27:46.375 --> 00:27:48.835
Well, it's cold right now anyway.

00:27:49.043 --> 00:27:50.627
We'll go in the spring.

00:27:58.924 --> 00:28:01.593
- Unbelievable.
- Oh, don't look. It's not finished.

00:28:01.759 --> 00:28:04.219
I wanted you to be surprised on Monday.

00:28:04.553 --> 00:28:06.095
I am.

00:28:07.388 --> 00:28:08.764
Julie, it's gorgeous.

00:28:11.057 --> 00:28:12.516
Did you do all this today?

00:28:13.100 --> 00:28:16.018
I was supposed to have Marissa
this weekend. That didn't happen.

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:17.769
I haven't heard from your father.

00:28:17.978 --> 00:28:20.813
So then I thought, why not work, right?
Take my mind off things.

00:28:21.021 --> 00:28:23.898
Have you heard from your father?
Have you talked to him today?

00:28:24.107 --> 00:28:26.525
No, no, not today, but...

00:28:27.692 --> 00:28:30.194
But what? Is he all right?
Did something happen?

00:28:30.402 --> 00:28:32.028
No, he's fine.

00:28:32.237 --> 00:28:33.613
- It's just...
- What?

00:28:35.405 --> 00:28:36.948
He doesn't like confrontation.

00:28:39.366 --> 00:28:42.118
Julie, you want to sit down?

00:28:42.452 --> 00:28:44.995
Why? What's going on?

00:28:51.290 --> 00:28:52.750
No.

00:28:53.417 --> 00:28:55.501
Is...?

00:28:55.710 --> 00:28:57.086
Is he breaking up with me?

00:29:00.921 --> 00:29:03.340
Or are you doing it for him?

00:29:03.673 --> 00:29:06.133
Kiki, I saw your car.

00:29:07.175 --> 00:29:08.801
Hello, darling.

00:29:09.510 --> 00:29:13.054
- I tried to call you earlier, but...
- Don't bother, Cal.

00:29:13.679 --> 00:29:17.140
Kirsten's already done
your dirty work for you.

00:29:18.182 --> 00:29:21.559
Because obviously you're not man enough
to do it yourself.

00:29:23.852 --> 00:29:26.521
- I'm sorry.
- You should be.

00:29:27.438 --> 00:29:29.439
God. I deserve so much better from you.

00:29:32.233 --> 00:29:33.817
From both of you.

00:29:35.902 --> 00:29:38.111
Enjoy your office. I quit.

00:29:47.826 --> 00:29:49.452
Hello, ladies. Seth.

00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:51.703
- Dad, don't call me a lady.
- Hey, Mr. Cohen.

00:29:51.912 --> 00:29:53.454
Hey, Sandy.

00:29:54.663 --> 00:29:57.040
So the comic-book education continues?

00:29:58.166 --> 00:29:59.458
Batman: The Animated Series.

00:29:59.666 --> 00:30:02.918
Yes. "Girls' Night Out," in which
Batgirl and Supergirl team up...

00:30:03.127 --> 00:30:06.045
...to combat the forces of evil
and delight Seth Cohen.

00:30:06.254 --> 00:30:08.630
Is Supergirl wearing Doc Martens?

00:30:09.297 --> 00:30:11.465
Yes. Yes, she is, Summer.

00:30:11.674 --> 00:30:15.385
And a midriff-baring T-shirt
and a miniskirt. It's excellent.

00:30:15.593 --> 00:30:18.470
- No wonder you like comics, Super-Perv.
- That's right.

00:30:19.429 --> 00:30:21.764
Dad, we were all gonna have lunch.
Is there...?

00:30:21.972 --> 00:30:25.808
- Can I see you? Now.
- Okay.

00:30:29.102 --> 00:30:30.227
What? What'd I do?

00:30:30.436 --> 00:30:32.145
You hurt that poor girl's feelings
out there.

00:30:32.812 --> 00:30:36.314
- Who, Dad, Summer? Please...
- No. No, Anna.

00:30:36.523 --> 00:30:38.316
- I didn't say a word to Anna.
- Exactly.

00:30:38.524 --> 00:30:41.776
How do you think that makes her feel,
you flirting with another girl?

00:30:41.985 --> 00:30:44.153
Dad, I was not flirting.

00:30:44.361 --> 00:30:47.029
- Seth.
- Dad. Summer and I are friends.

00:30:47.196 --> 00:30:50.115
- That's not what it looked like.
- I'm not talking about this.

00:30:50.323 --> 00:30:53.075
Of course not. No one's talking
to me about anything lately.

00:30:53.242 --> 00:30:55.743
- Lf you want to flirt...
- Why are we talking about this?

00:30:55.952 --> 00:30:58.537
Because I'm your father
and I'm responsible for you.

00:30:58.745 --> 00:31:02.331
And if I see something's going on
with you, we are gonna talk about it.

00:31:04.290 --> 00:31:06.583
Do you think that this is about me...

00:31:06.792 --> 00:31:08.251
...or could this be about Ryan?

00:31:09.335 --> 00:31:12.003
No. It's about you.

00:31:14.130 --> 00:31:15.672
Okay.

00:31:15.881 --> 00:31:18.799
But just in case
it's a little bit about Ryan...

00:31:19.925 --> 00:31:22.385
...I think he'll come to you
when he's ready.

00:31:29.681 --> 00:31:31.599
- Hey, Mrs. Cooper.
- Hey.

00:31:31.932 --> 00:31:33.475
You all right?

00:31:34.017 --> 00:31:38.228
Hard day. Come on in.
I'll get Marissa's things for you.

00:31:42.231 --> 00:31:46.483
Well, I have to say, I'm very impressed
that you and Marissa are still friends.

00:31:47.067 --> 00:31:51.486
- Yeah, I'm impressed she forgave me.
- Maybe one day she'll forgive me too.

00:31:51.695 --> 00:31:53.404
For what?

00:31:55.572 --> 00:31:59.283
Well, I haven't exactly
been the best mom, have I?

00:31:59.950 --> 00:32:04.995
Or the best wife, or the best girlfriend,
for that matter.

00:32:06.120 --> 00:32:07.580
You and Mr. Nichol?

00:32:07.788 --> 00:32:09.998
Yeah. It's over.

00:32:10.457 --> 00:32:12.791
Which means that...

00:32:13.083 --> 00:32:15.251
...in the past six months...

00:32:15.460 --> 00:32:18.795
...I've lost my husband, my daughter...

00:32:19.004 --> 00:32:21.422
...my boyfriend and my job.

00:32:22.172 --> 00:32:25.049
I'm sorry.
I shouldn't be telling you all this.

00:32:25.257 --> 00:32:26.842
No, no, it's okay.

00:32:27.050 --> 00:32:29.760
The past few months have been rough
on everybody.

00:32:29.927 --> 00:32:31.094
Yeah.

00:32:31.303 --> 00:32:33.179
Yeah, they have.

00:32:36.723 --> 00:32:38.683
Thank you for listening.

00:32:38.891 --> 00:32:41.184
I haven't had anyone to talk to in so long.

00:32:41.393 --> 00:32:46.354
Well, you can talk to me.
I don't know what good it'll do, but...

00:32:48.605 --> 00:32:49.773
Hey.

00:33:05.574 --> 00:33:07.242
You should go.

00:33:07.450 --> 00:33:09.660
Marissa's waiting.

00:33:20.208 --> 00:33:23.586
Hi, I'm Marissa Cooper. I'm staying
in the penthouse with Oliver Trask.

00:33:23.794 --> 00:33:26.129
I was wondering if someone
dropped off a bag for me.

00:33:26.337 --> 00:33:28.255
Sorry. One moment.

00:33:28.464 --> 00:33:31.382
Thank you for calling. This is Natalie.
Can you hold, please?

00:33:32.675 --> 00:33:34.884
- Let me check for you, Miss Cooper.
- Natalie?

00:33:35.093 --> 00:33:38.261
- Do you know Oliver Trask?
- Yeah, since he was just a little guy.

00:33:38.470 --> 00:33:41.930
I used to babysit him.
You don't want to know how old I am.

00:33:42.597 --> 00:33:45.433
Your last name isn't Bishop, is it?

00:33:46.100 --> 00:33:47.392
Yes, why do you ask?

00:33:55.939 --> 00:33:57.190
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:33:57.398 --> 00:33:59.149
I was just calling your cell.

00:33:59.358 --> 00:34:02.026
Where'd you go? I got out
of the shower, and you were gone.

00:34:02.235 --> 00:34:05.237
I just went downstairs to see
if they had my bag, but they didn't.

00:34:05.445 --> 00:34:08.030
You didn't have to do that.
They'll bring it up.

00:34:09.573 --> 00:34:12.241
- You okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

00:34:12.408 --> 00:34:13.659
It's just...

00:34:15.827 --> 00:34:18.370
It's just, the weirdest thing happened.

00:34:18.578 --> 00:34:21.955
You know the concierge at the
front desk? Her name's Natalie.

00:34:22.289 --> 00:34:25.458
Natalie Bishop.
The same as your ex-girlfriend, right?

00:34:25.666 --> 00:34:29.293
- It's just, how weird is that?
- I know what you're thinking, but...

00:34:29.502 --> 00:34:33.421
- There is no ex-girlfriend, is there?
- Marissa, I can explain.

00:34:33.629 --> 00:34:35.255
- I have to go.
- No, no. Please.

00:34:35.464 --> 00:34:39.758
Okay. I'm so sorry. I always do this.
Why do I always do this?

00:34:39.967 --> 00:34:42.218
- Oliver, stop it.
- Damn it!

00:34:42.427 --> 00:34:44.219
- Oliver, stop.
- Okay.

00:34:44.428 --> 00:34:47.179
All right? It's okay.
I'm not going anywhere.

00:34:47.346 --> 00:34:50.765
So why don't you just go get changed,
and then we can go?

00:34:50.974 --> 00:34:53.934
- I'm so sorry.
- It's okay.

00:34:54.642 --> 00:34:56.185
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:35:06.233 --> 00:35:07.442
Come on. Pick up.

00:35:20.450 --> 00:35:22.118
- Hello?
- Ryan, it's me.

00:35:22.952 --> 00:35:26.246
- What's going on? Where are you?
- At the hotel. I can't talk right now.

00:35:26.454 --> 00:35:29.748
It's Oliver, he's... You were right.
And now he won't let me leave.

00:35:29.956 --> 00:35:31.332
Hang up!

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.293
Hang up the phone. Please?

00:35:36.544 --> 00:35:37.711
Give me the phone.

00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:39.754
- What are you doing?
- What's going on?

00:35:39.962 --> 00:35:42.130
Please, give me the phone.

00:35:44.257 --> 00:35:45.424
Bye, Ryan.

00:35:52.012 --> 00:35:55.764
It's too bad that Summer couldn't stay.
We have so much food.

00:35:55.972 --> 00:35:59.141
- Never fear, Mom. Anna's here.
- You noticed.

00:35:59.350 --> 00:36:02.477
- Hey, Seth, why don't you go get Ryan.
- Okay.

00:36:02.685 --> 00:36:04.436
- Hey, will you come with me?
- Yeah.

00:36:04.645 --> 00:36:08.314
Sure, maybe then we can be alone
for, like, 10 seconds.

00:36:10.690 --> 00:36:12.900
Hey. I'm sorry about the Summer thing.

00:36:13.108 --> 00:36:15.610
You know how excited I get
turning people on to comics.

00:36:15.818 --> 00:36:18.320
I know how excited you get
turning Summer on, yeah.

00:36:18.528 --> 00:36:19.821
Okay. That's not fair.

00:36:20.029 --> 00:36:22.864
- I thought we were all friends.
- No. She's your friend.

00:36:23.031 --> 00:36:26.200
I am your girlfriend. There's a difference.
Or there should be.

00:36:27.992 --> 00:36:29.869
Hey! Food's here.

00:36:30.077 --> 00:36:32.537
- Where you going?
- I think Marissa's in trouble.

00:36:32.745 --> 00:36:34.538
- Give me the keys.
- I have to go, okay?

00:36:34.747 --> 00:36:35.997
Give me the keys!

00:36:36.206 --> 00:36:39.958
- You said I could come to you for help.
- Give me the keys!

00:36:42.627 --> 00:36:44.378
I'll drive.

00:36:46.796 --> 00:36:48.797
I'm sorry, okay? I'm so sorry.

00:36:49.006 --> 00:36:51.132
I heard you on the phone,
and I didn't know what to do.

00:36:51.340 --> 00:36:53.842
That's okay. So why don't you
just put the gun down.

00:36:54.092 --> 00:36:56.052
- We can talk about it.
- No, you'll leave.

00:36:56.260 --> 00:36:59.012
- Oliver. I have to go some time.
- What? To him?

00:36:59.220 --> 00:37:00.429
To him, right?

00:37:00.638 --> 00:37:02.431
- What about me?
- You and I are friends.

00:37:02.639 --> 00:37:05.099
- We will always be friends.
- Friends?!

00:37:05.307 --> 00:37:07.559
Friends, Marissa?! I'm in love with you!

00:37:07.767 --> 00:37:10.728
How could you not know that?
I've always been.

00:37:12.812 --> 00:37:16.856
You're the one who gets me.
The only one who gets me.

00:37:17.398 --> 00:37:19.775
You're the only thing
in my life that I love.

00:37:19.983 --> 00:37:22.360
Then why would you want to hurt me?

00:37:22.568 --> 00:37:25.320
I don't. I never would.

00:37:27.363 --> 00:37:29.322
This isn't for you. It's for me.

00:37:30.073 --> 00:37:32.658
Because if you leave,
I'll have nothing else to live for.

00:37:33.784 --> 00:37:36.994
So you have to promise me
you will not leave.

00:37:45.041 --> 00:37:47.334
There's no answer.
They're not picking up.

00:37:49.543 --> 00:37:52.462
Excuse me. My name's Sandy Cohen.
We got an emergency call...

00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:55.589
...from the penthouse 20 minutes ago,
and now no one's answering.

00:37:55.797 --> 00:37:57.757
Is there any chance you could let us in?

00:37:57.965 --> 00:38:00.717
I'm sorry. Without permission,
we're really not able to.

00:38:00.884 --> 00:38:04.720
Please, we have a friend up there
in trouble. If you could just... Wait.

00:38:04.928 --> 00:38:06.221
Wait. You're Natalie?

00:38:08.263 --> 00:38:09.723
Natalie Bishop?

00:38:10.890 --> 00:38:12.766
Are you a friend of Oliver's?

00:38:18.853 --> 00:38:21.147
Oliver, you there? It's Natalie.

00:38:23.356 --> 00:38:25.941
- Oliver, I'm coming in.
- No, no. That's okay.

00:38:26.150 --> 00:38:28.568
I'm fine. I just got out of the shower.

00:38:28.776 --> 00:38:30.694
Oliver, please.

00:38:31.903 --> 00:38:33.613
I guess he's fine.

00:38:33.821 --> 00:38:35.864
Well, thanks for checking.

00:38:36.073 --> 00:38:37.532
We'll go.

00:38:37.740 --> 00:38:40.200
No, no. Marissa?

00:38:45.287 --> 00:38:46.579
Marissa!

00:38:48.163 --> 00:38:49.831
All right. Let's go.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:51.290
Ryan, he's got a gun!

00:38:51.666 --> 00:38:54.542
- Let's go.
- Why did you do that?

00:38:54.751 --> 00:38:56.335
- Why?
- I'm sorry.

00:38:56.544 --> 00:38:59.212
Please just put the gun away
and let them in.

00:38:59.379 --> 00:39:01.422
- Sir, don't move!
- Put the gun down.

00:39:01.630 --> 00:39:02.881
Or what? You're gonna shoot me?

00:39:03.840 --> 00:39:05.799
- Let me save you the trouble.
- Come on, son.

00:39:06.008 --> 00:39:08.843
- You don't want to do that.
- Put the gun down. Now.

00:39:11.470 --> 00:39:14.472
- I'm sorry.
- Oliver, put the gun down, man.

00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:17.098
Why, man? I'm doing you a favor.

00:39:17.307 --> 00:39:19.808
Why would you want to do that?
You hate me.

00:39:21.726 --> 00:39:24.645
That's right, you do this,
you won't hurt me.

00:39:24.853 --> 00:39:27.480
You'll hurt Marissa,
the one person that cares about you.

00:39:27.646 --> 00:39:29.773
And I know you don't want to do that.

00:39:30.982 --> 00:39:32.775
Oliver, put the gun down, man.

00:39:34.359 --> 00:39:36.444
You don't know anything about me, man.

00:39:36.944 --> 00:39:39.445
I know what it's like
to be abandoned by your parents...

00:39:39.821 --> 00:39:41.989
...your friends...

00:39:42.489 --> 00:39:45.241
...to have no one in your life
who believes in you.

00:39:48.159 --> 00:39:50.828
But you put the gun down,
you get a second chance.

00:40:04.586 --> 00:40:06.337
That's it. Just put it down.

00:40:06.671 --> 00:40:10.256
- I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
- It's okay.

00:40:27.309 --> 00:40:29.894
Marissa's okay. Her mom's got her.

00:40:30.352 --> 00:40:33.021
And the police are taking Oliver
to the hospital.

00:40:34.730 --> 00:40:37.899
I'm gonna clean up the pool house
before they get here.

00:40:40.817 --> 00:40:42.735
I should give Summer a call.

00:40:42.944 --> 00:40:44.986
What? Why?

00:40:45.195 --> 00:40:48.364
- To let her know Marissa's okay.
- She doesn't know Marissa's not okay.

00:40:48.572 --> 00:40:51.074
- Don't you think she'd want to know?
- You know what?

00:40:51.741 --> 00:40:53.617
- Call her. I'm leaving.
- Anna, wait.

00:40:53.825 --> 00:40:55.827
Just wait.
This huge thing just happened.

00:40:56.035 --> 00:40:58.453
And the first thing you do
is decide to call Summer?

00:41:00.121 --> 00:41:02.080
Come on, Seth.

00:41:04.624 --> 00:41:05.916
Look...

00:41:07.876 --> 00:41:09.960
...I think you're a great guy.

00:41:11.128 --> 00:41:15.255
But I'm not gonna stand here and pretend
like I'm your girlfriend when I'm not.

00:41:16.464 --> 00:41:18.299
At least not anymore.

00:41:20.133 --> 00:41:21.926
I'll see you in school.

00:41:36.852 --> 00:41:38.311
Hi.

00:41:39.187 --> 00:41:42.022
I was wondering where my copy
of Kavalier and Klay went.

00:41:42.231 --> 00:41:45.524
You gave it to me. You said I couldn't
be your friend until I read it.

00:41:45.733 --> 00:41:47.192
And have you?

00:41:47.359 --> 00:41:49.235
I've been a little distracted.

00:41:49.610 --> 00:41:51.403
Well, it's a good story, Ryan.

00:41:51.611 --> 00:41:54.738
It's the tale of two young men
who couldn't be more different...

00:41:55.280 --> 00:41:57.699
...but they learn to overcome
their differences.

00:41:57.907 --> 00:42:00.242
They team up and essentially...

00:42:00.450 --> 00:42:03.577
...become brothers,
not unlike you and me.

00:42:05.287 --> 00:42:06.954
Except that I blew it.

00:42:08.539 --> 00:42:11.207
- It's okay.
- No, it's not.

00:42:12.041 --> 00:42:16.210
Ever since the day you got here,
you have totally had my back.

00:42:16.419 --> 00:42:22.256
And I promise you, from now on,
I will never fail you again.

00:42:22.464 --> 00:42:24.048
I'm so sorry.

00:42:33.596 --> 00:42:35.347
Do you want to tell me
about your night?

00:42:35.556 --> 00:42:39.975
Or, since I already heard about it,
could we skip to my breakup with Anna?

00:42:40.183 --> 00:42:41.726
Really? Anna broke up with you?

00:42:41.893 --> 00:42:44.019
Why would you just assume
Anna broke up with me?

00:42:44.353 --> 00:42:46.813
- Seth, come on.
- What does that mean?

00:42:47.021 --> 00:42:48.564
What, she didn't break up with you?

00:42:48.772 --> 00:42:51.024
She did. But you're supposed
to have my back here.

00:42:51.232 --> 00:42:54.192
So the three of us...
